{"name":"Spiced Tea","hex":"#ab6162","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spiced","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having spice added, spicy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of spice"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiced"},{"term":"tea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Temiar."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The tea plant (Camellia sinensis);  a variety of this plant.","The dried leaves or buds of the tea plant;  a variety of such leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Masala chai","blocks":[{"text":"Masala chai is a popular beverage originating from India. It is made by adding aromatic herbs and spices to chai, which is made from brewing black tea in milk and water, and sweetening with sugar, often using aeration techniques only performed by masters or \"tevanas\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Chai_In_Sakora.jpg/330px-Chai_In_Sakora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masala_chai","wikidata":"Q877661"},{"title":"Spice","blocks":[{"text":"In the culinary arts, a spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavouring or colouring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavouring or as a garnish. Spices and herbs are both seasonings. \nSpices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics, or perfume production. They are usually classified into spices, spice seeds, and herbal categories. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Plant-based sweeteners such as sugar are not considered spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Spices1.jpg/330px-Spices1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice","wikidata":"Q42527"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Chai-Kwon-Do.jpg/500px-Chai-Kwon-Do.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Chai-Kwon-Do.jpg/500px-Chai-Kwon-Do.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Typical spices used for masala chai","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChai-Kwon-Do.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Teamaking.JPG/500px-Teamaking.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Teamaking.JPG/500px-Teamaking.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy in Mysore preparing masala chai: As it is prepared by decoction, preparation usually includes straining tea from the solids.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeamaking.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Contents_of_a_bag_of_chai_tea.jpg/500px-Contents_of_a_bag_of_chai_tea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb